{
  "id": "module-3-python-comments",
  "title": "Module 3: Python Comments",
  "description": "Lessons 3.1 through 3.5",
  "initiallyExpanded": false,
  "lessons": [
    {
      "id": "lesson-3-1-introduction-to-comments",
      "number": "3.1",
      "title": "Introduction to Comments",
      "summary": "As you start writing more code, you might want to add short explanations inside your program—not for the computer, but for yourself or anyone else reading it later.",
      "status": "available",
      "estimatedMinutes": 5,
      "tags": [
        "python-comments"
      ],
      "blocks": [
        {
          "id": "page-3-1-paragraph-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": "As you start writing more code, you might want to add short explanations inside your program—not for the computer, but for yourself or anyone else reading it later.",
          "format": "plain"
        },
        {
          "id": "page-3-1-paragraph-2",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": "Suppose you write this line in your code:",
          "format": "plain"
        },
        {
          "id": "page-3-1-code-3",
          "type": "code",
          "language": "python",
          "code": "print(34.0)",
          "caption": "Example"
        },
        {
          "id": "page-3-1-paragraph-4",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": "This will simply print the number 34.0.",
          "format": "plain"
        },
        {
          "id": "page-3-1-paragraph-5",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": "Now let's say you want to explain what this number means. Maybe it's the temperature or the result of a calculation. You might try writing it like this:",
          "format": "plain"
        },
        {
          "id": "page-3-1-code-6",
          "type": "code",
          "language": "python",
          "code": "print(34.0) this shows the temperature",
          "caption": "Example"
        },
        {
          "id": "page-3-1-paragraph-7",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": "But Python won't understand that extra text, and it will give you an error.",
          "format": "plain"
        },
        {
          "id": "page-3-1-paragraph-8",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": "So how do you include extra information in your code without breaking it?",
          "format": "plain"
        },
        {
          "id": "page-3-1-paragraph-9",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": "That's where comments come in. Comments let you add helpful notes right inside your code, and Python will simply ignore them when running the program.",
          "format": "plain"
        },
        {
          "id": "page-3-1-paragraph-10",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": "You don't need to worry about how to write them just yet.",
          "format": "plain"
        },
        {
          "id": "page-3-1-heading-11",
          "type": "heading",
          "level": 3,
          "text": "Click Next Lesson to learn how to add comments properly in Python."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "lesson-3-2-python-comments",
      "number": "3.2",
      "title": "Python Comments",
      "summary": "In Python, we use the # symbol to write comments in our code.",
      "status": "available",
      "estimatedMinutes": 5,
      "tags": [
        "python-comments"
      ],
      "blocks": [
        {
          "id": "page-3-2-paragraph-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": "In Python, we use the # symbol to write comments in our code.",
          "format": "plain"
        },
        {
          "id": "page-3-2-paragraph-2",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": "On the last page, we saw that writing something like this:",
          "format": "plain"
        },
        {
          "id": "page-3-2-code-3",
          "type": "code",
          "language": "python",
          "code": "print(34.0) this shows the temperature",
          "caption": "Example"
        },
        {
          "id": "page-3-2-paragraph-4",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": "will give you an error. That's because Python tries to read everything on the line, and it doesn't know what to do with the extra text.",
          "format": "plain"
        },
        {
          "id": "page-3-2-paragraph-5",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": "But sometimes, you do want to write a quick note to explain what a line of code is doing. To do that without causing an error, you can use a comment.",
          "format": "plain"
        },
        {
          "id": "page-3-2-paragraph-6",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": "Just add a # before the explanation, like this:",
          "format": "plain"
        },
        {
          "id": "page-3-2-code-7",
          "type": "code",
          "language": "python",
          "code": "print(34.0) # This shows the temperature",
          "caption": "Example"
        },
        {
          "id": "page-3-2-paragraph-8",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": "Now Python will run the first part (print(34.0)) and completely ignore anything after the #. In fact, Python skips any line that starts with #—it doesn't run it, and it won't appear in the output at all.",
          "format": "plain"
        },
        {
          "id": "page-3-2-paragraph-9",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": "Next, you'll look at more examples of comments.",
          "format": "plain"
        },
        {
          "id": "page-3-2-heading-10",
          "type": "heading",
          "level": 3,
          "text": "Click Next Lesson to continue."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "lesson-3-3-understanding-python-comments",
      "number": "3.3",
      "title": "Understanding Python Comments",
      "summary": "Let's look at another example:",
      "status": "available",
      "estimatedMinutes": 5,
      "tags": [
        "python-comments"
      ],
      "blocks": [
        {
          "id": "page-3-3-paragraph-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": "Let's look at another example:",
          "format": "plain"
        },
        {
          "id": "page-3-3-code-2",
          "type": "code",
          "language": "python",
          "code": "# Print a number\nprint(6)\nprint(8) # Print another number\n# Print third number\nprint(88.3)",
          "caption": "Example"
        },
        {
          "id": "page-3-3-paragraph-3",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": "This code has three comments:",
          "format": "plain"
        },
        {
          "id": "page-3-3-code-4",
          "type": "code",
          "language": "python",
          "code": "# Print a number\n# Print another number\n# Print third number",
          "caption": "Example"
        },
        {
          "id": "page-3-3-paragraph-5",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": "Python skips all of them when running the program. Only the print() lines are executed.",
          "format": "plain"
        },
        {
          "id": "page-3-3-paragraph-6",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": "So this is the same as:",
          "format": "plain"
        },
        {
          "id": "page-3-3-code-7",
          "type": "code",
          "language": "python",
          "code": "print(6)\nprint(8)\nprint(88.3)",
          "caption": "Example"
        },
        {
          "id": "page-3-3-paragraph-8",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": "The output will be:",
          "format": "plain"
        },
        {
          "id": "page-3-3-code-9",
          "type": "code",
          "language": "python",
          "code": "6\n8\n88.3",
          "caption": "Example"
        },
        {
          "id": "page-3-3-paragraph-10",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": "The comments help explain the code, but do not affect what the program does.",
          "format": "plain"
        },
        {
          "id": "page-3-3-image-11",
          "type": "image",
          "src": "/assets/courses/python-course/python-course-image-06.png",
          "alt": "Idea Emoji",
          "caption": "Idea Emoji",
          "loading": "lazy"
        },
        {
          "id": "page-3-3-note-12",
          "type": "note",
          "title": "Note",
          "content": "You'll find comments throughout this course, which we'll use to explain the code examples.",
          "format": "plain"
        },
        {
          "id": "page-3-3-paragraph-13",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": "Next, you'll check your understanding with two short quizzes on identifying comments and understanding their effect.",
          "format": "plain"
        },
        {
          "id": "page-3-3-paragraph-14",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": "Click Next Lesson to continue.",
          "format": "plain"
        }
      ]
    },
